        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement US, Israel war on Iran World Middle East Iran to turn bombed girls’ school into museum commemorating US ‘crimes’ At least 168 pupils, 26 teachers and four parents were killed in the attack in the southern city of Minab on February 28 2 -MIN READ 2 -MIN 1 dpa Published: 6:19pm, 16 Mar 2026 Iran plans to convert the girls’ school that was bombed on the first day of the war into a museum commemorating the nearly 200 victims of the strike. “This school is a living document of the Americans’ willingness to commit crimes and must be registered and documented for preservation in the historical memory of the Iranian people,” the Iranian government said in a statement issued on Monday. At least 168 pupils aged between seven and 12 years old, 26 teachers and four parents were killed in the attack in the southern city of Minab on February 28. Advertisement Various media reports have pointed the finger at the United States as being responsible for the attack. Citing confidential sources, The New York Times and CNN have reported that the preliminary results of an investigation indicate US responsibility. The US is said to have targeted an Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps base to which the school building previously belonged. Outdated location data reportedly led to the fatal error. Advertisement Further details about the plans for the museum were not initially provided. The school is to be rebuilt elsewhere in memory of the victims. Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
